cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "COMPAS IFC: A front-end data model for IFC"
abstract: >-
  COMPAS IFC is an open-source Python toolkit that provides a small,
  intentional front-end data model over the Industry Foundation Classes
  (IFC). It couples geometric representations to executable geometry
  kernels, materialises the IFC spatial hierarchy as an explicit tree with
  integrated placement, exposes non-hierarchical relationships as a separate
  interaction graph, and validates custom element metadata against Pydantic
  schemas. It is the software artefact accompanying Chapter 4 of the doctoral
  thesis "Future Data Models for AEC: From Simplicity for Humans to
  Interoperability by AI".
